Usage: /usr/sbin/chromeos-firmwareupdate [options]

-V:              print human readable version information
--manifest:      print machine readable (JSON) version information
--unpack DEST:   unpack the contents to DEST
--repack SRC:    repack with contents from SRC


If no options are given, prints firmware info and exits.
Other options will be passed to 'futility update' command:


Usage:  futility update [OPTIONS]

Updates firmware in one of the following modes (default to recovery):
  autoupdate:	Update RW[A|B], or recovery if RO changed.
  recovery:  	Update RW[A&B], (RO, RO:GBB[keys] - if RO changed)
  factory:   	Update RW[A&B],  RO, RO:GBB[keys,flags]

Note: firmware sections with PRESERVE flags like VPD and
      HWID in GBB are always preserved.
      GBB flags are preserved in autoupdate and recovery modes.

OPTIONS:

-i, --image=FILE    	AP (host) firmware image (image.bin)
-e, --ec_image=FILE 	EC firmware image (i.e, ec.bin)
-t, --try           	Try A/B update on reboot if possible
-a, --archive=PATH  	Read resources from archive
    --model=MODEL   	Specify or override the model name in the
                    	archive. This is useful for flashing over
                    	servo, where crosid is not available.
    --frid=FRID     	Specify FRID to match in identity.csv
    --sku-id=SKU_ID 	Specify SKU ID to match in identity.csv
                    	Specifying both --frid and --sku-id is
                    	sufficient to decide the model name
                    	from identity.csv
    --unpack=DIR    	Extracts archive to DIR
    --fast          	Reduce read cycles and do not verify
    --quirks=LIST   	Specify the quirks to apply
    --list-quirks   	Print all available quirks
-m, --mode=MODE     	Run updater in the specified mode
    --manifest      	Scan the archive to print a manifest in JSON
    --parseable-manifest
                    	Scan the archive to print a manifest
                    	in shell-parseable format
    --check-fwid    	Compare firmware id before performing
                    	an update. Skip the update if the versions are
                    	the same.
-p, --programmer=PRG	Change AP (host) flashrom programmer
    --ccd_without_servod[=SERIAL] 	Flash via CCD without servod
    --emulate=FILE  	Emulate system firmware using file
    --servo         	Flash using Servo (v2, v4, micro, ...)
    --servo_port=PRT	Override servod port, implies --servo

 * Option --manifest requires either -a,--archive or -i,--image
   With -i,--image additional images are accepted with options
   -e,--ec_image.
 * If both --manifest and --fast are specified, the updater
   will not scan the archive and simply dump the previously
   cached manifest (may be out-dated) from the archive.
   Works only with -a,--archive option.
 * Use of -p,--programmer with option other than 'internal',
   or with --ccd effectively disables ability to update EC
   firmware images.
 * Emulation works only with the AP (host) firmware image, and
   does not support the EC firmware image.
 * Model detection with option --detect-model-only requires
   archive path -a,--archive
 * The --quirks provides a set of options to override the
   default behavior. Run --list-quirks to get the options,
   and --quirks OPTION to turn on. To disable a quirk that
   was default turned on from the firmware image CBFS, do
   --quirks OPTION=0 to turn off.

Legacy and compatibility options:
    --factory       	Alias for --mode=factory
    --force         	Force update (skip checking contents)
    --output_dir=DIR	Specify the target for --mode=output
    --unlock_me     	(deprecated) Unlock the Intel ME before flashing
    --signature_id=S	(deprecated) Same as --model

Debugging and testing options:
    --wp=1|0        	Specify write protection status
    --host_only     	Update only AP (host) firmware
    --detect-model-only	Detect model by reading the FRID and exit
    --gbb_flags=FLAG	Override new GBB flags
    --sys_props=LIST	List of system properties to override
-d, --debug         	Print debugging messages
-v, --verbose       	Print verbose messages
